.git
.gitignore
# Any depth, not just the context root: `COPY app ./app` would otherwise ship
# app/__pycache__, i.e. bytecode from whatever the build host last ran.
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
# Any depth, for the same reason and since #108: `tools/screenshots/.venv` is a venv the
# screenshot tool's README tells a maintainer to create inside the checkout, and a bare
# `.venv` matches only the context root, so every build would ship Playwright's bundled
# driver and browser wrapper to the daemon.
**/.venv
.env
.idea
.vscode
